    <string name="captantan_pointer_speed">Trackpad pointer speed (%)</string>
    <string name="captantan_touch_scroll">Touch scrolling</string>
    <string name="captantan_touch_scroll_natural">Natural: the content follows the fingers</string>
    <string name="captantan_touch_scroll_traditional">Traditional: the fingers move the scroll bar</string>
    <string name="captantan_touch_drag">One-finger drag in direct touch</string>
    <string name="captantan_touch_drag_scroll">Scrolls, as on a Windows touchscreen</string>
    <string name="captantan_touch_drag_off">Does nothing (upstream)</string>
    <string name="captantan_touch_note">Direct touch: tap to click, hold a moment and then drag to select or move a window. Zoomed in, a one-finger drag moves the view. Trackpad: move one finger anywhere to move the pointer. Tap to click, tap with two fingers to right-click, drag two fingers to scroll and pinch to zoom. To drag or select, tap and then touch again and move. A mouse and a touchpad work as always. The session bar\'s input mode button switches modes during a session. Pen: as a pen, the host gets the pen itself, with pressure, tilt, the side button and the eraser, and does with it what it does with its own pens (Windows hosts; elsewhere the pen is a pointer). As a pointer, hovering moves the mouse pointer, a tap clicks, a quick drag scrolls, hold a moment and then drag to select, and a tap with the side button held is a right click.</string>
